# =============================================================================
#  §10 (s10) — DATA vs MACHINERY boundary (default-deny)
# =============================================================================
#  This repo ingests personal notes, repo snapshots and PDFs that routinely
#  contain secrets (DB creds, tokens, bastion access). To make a leak
#  structurally hard, tracking is DEFAULT-DENY:
#
#    * MACHINERY  — the system itself (code, tests, prompts, config TEMPLATES,
#      docs, the eval harness). Tracked. Allow-listed by name below.
#    * DATA       — anything the system reads or produces (raw/ compiled/ state/
#      logs/ review/ eval results, the real config, the .env, samples). NEVER
#      tracked. Any NEW top-level entry is ignored by default, so a future data
#      dir (cache/, inbox/, embeddings/…) can't silently get committed.
#
#  To track a NEW machinery path you must consciously add a `!` line here. That
#  deliberate step is the safeguard. When in doubt: it's data — leave it out.
#
#  NOTE: .gitignore keeps DATA out of git. It does NOT stop a secret pasted into
#  a tracked machinery file (docs!) — that's what the pre-commit secret scan
#  (scripts/scan_secrets.py via hooks/) is for. Install: git config core.hooksPath hooks
# -----------------------------------------------------------------------------

# 1) Default-deny: ignore every top-level entry...
/*

# 2) ...then re-include MACHINERY only.
#    Root files:
!/.gitignore
!/README.md
!/CLAUDE.md
!/LICENSE
!/requirements.txt
!/requirements-dev.txt

#    Machinery directories (their contents are tracked):
!/scripts/
!/tests/
!/prompts/
!/config/
!/docs/
!/evals/
!/hooks/

# 3) Carve DATA back out of otherwise-tracked machinery dirs.
#    Eval *results* are regenerated data; only the harness + golden cases ship.
/evals/results/
#    Eval *candidates* are raw captured transcripts (may carry client data) staged
#    for triage; they stay local-only.
/evals/candidates/
#    Your real golden cases are data (they quote your own sessions); ship
#    evals/cases.example.jsonl instead and copy it to cases.jsonl locally.
/evals/cases.jsonl
#    Real curation/project config is data; ship the .example templates instead.
/config/topics.yaml
/config/source_projects.yaml
#    Hook-tuning observation logs are data (they quote your own prompts/sessions);
#    only the README/template ships. auto-audit.md is written by the nightly
#    audit_hooks.py, the other two by hand as misfires are observed.
/docs/hook-tuning/auto-audit.md
/docs/hook-tuning/memory-injection.md
/docs/hook-tuning/correction-capture.md

# 4) Belt-and-suspenders: name the known data + secret paths explicitly, so the
#    intent stays documented even if the default-deny block above is ever loosened.
/.env
/raw/
/compiled/
/review/
/state/
/logs/
/sample.pdf
/sample_local_llm_note.md
/.hermes/

# 5) Tooling / OS noise (also covered by default-deny; kept for clarity)
__pycache__/
*.pyc
*.egg-info/
.pytest_cache/
.venv/
.DS_Store
Thumbs.db
